description:
Define the data structures the agent loop operates on. Ref: Pi's AgentMessage/AgentToolCall types.
- include/cclaw.h:
  - enum Role { ROLE_SYSTEM, ROLE_USER, ROLE_ASSISTANT, ROLE_TOOL }
  - struct Message { Role role; char *content; char *tool_call_id; ToolCall *tool_calls; int tool_call_count; }
  - struct ToolCall { char *id; char *name; char *arguments_json; }
  - struct ToolResult { char *tool_call_id; char *content; bool is_error; }
  - struct Config { char *api_key; char *base_url; char *model; char *system_prompt; int max_history; int max_tool_iterations; }
  - struct AgentContext { Message *messages; int msg_count; int msg_capacity; Arena *arena; Config *config; }
- test/test_types.c: create context, add messages, verify counts
TDD: tests first.

Define foundational types and memory management:

Arena allocator (include/arena.h, src/arena.c):
- Simple bump allocator with linked list of blocks
- arena_create(initial_size) / arena_alloc(arena, size) / arena_reset(arena) / arena_destroy(arena)
- Per-conversation: allocate an arena at turn start, reset at turn end
- No individual frees needed within a turn

Core types (include/cclaw.h):
- Message: { role (system/user/assistant/tool), content, tool_call_id, tool_calls[] }
- ToolCall: { id, name, arguments_json }
- ToolResult: { tool_call_id, content, is_error }
- AgentContext: { messages[], message_count, arena, config, curl_handle, db }
- Config: { telegram_token, llm_api_key, llm_base_url, llm_model, system_prompt, db_path, max_turns }

String handling:
- All strings are arena-allocated or static
- Helper: arena_strdup, arena_sprintf
- No strdup/malloc for transient per-turn data

Parse chat completions response. Ref: Pi collects tool_calls from assistant message content blocks.
- src/llm.c: llm_parse_response(json_str, arena) -> LlmResponse {content, tool_calls[], tool_call_count, finish_reason, error_msg}
- Handle: choices[0].message.content, choices[0].message.tool_calls[].{id,function.name,function.arguments}, choices[0].finish_reason
- Handle error response: {error:{message,type}}
- test/test_llm_response.c: parse sample responses (text-only, with tool_calls, error). Use fixture JSON strings.
TDD: pure unit test with hardcoded JSON fixtures.
